<section class="craft-v2-compare"><div class="craft-v2-wrap"><div class="craft-v2-compare-head craft-v2-reveal"><div><p class="craft-v2-eyebrow">Plate 01 · Comparison frame</p><h2>Compare the <em>conditions.</em></h2></div><p>This matrix defines what a real study needs to report. Values remain unknown until measurements are collected under a documented protocol.</p></div><div class="craft-v2-matrix-wrap craft-v2-reveal" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable drying method comparison"><table class="craft-v2-matrix"><thead><tr><th>Criterion</th><th>Traditional</th><th>Improved</th><th>Hot air</th><th>Solar hybrid</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Temperature control</th><td>To measure</td><td>To measure</td><td>Set-point capable</td><td>Weather dependent</td></tr><tr><th>Smoke exposure</th><td>To measure</td><td>To measure</td><td>Designed without smoke</td><td>Depends on backup heat</td></tr><tr><th>Energy and fuel</th><td>To record</td><td>To record</td><td>To record</td><td>To record</td></tr><tr><th>Drying time</th><td>To measure</td><td>To measure</td><td>To measure</td><td>To measure</td></tr><tr><th>Local practicality</th><td>Interview</td><td>Interview</td><td>Interview</td><td>Interview</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section class="craft-v2-alternative"><div class="craft-v2-alternative-image" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="craft-v2-alternative-copy craft-v2-reveal"><p class="craft-v2-eyebrow">Concept study · Alternative dryer</p><h2>Control is useful only if it can <em>travel.</em></h2><p>A technically successful dryer may still fail if it cannot be built, powered, repaired or operated where cardamom is grown. Equipment design and field practicality belong in the same evaluation.</p><p class="craft-v2-concept-note">AI-generated equipment concept · not an installed machine</p></div></section><section class="craft-v2-protocol"><div class="craft-v2-wrap craft-v2-protocol-grid"><div class="craft-v2-reveal"><p class="craft-v2-eyebrow">Entry 04 · Protocol</p><h2>What the laboratory should <em>see.</em></h2><p>The final protocol must be defined with qualified laboratory partners and relevant standards. This design shows the evidence categories the page will eventually report.</p></div><div class="craft-v2-tests craft-v2-reveal"><article><b>01 · Stability</b><h3>Moisture</h3><p>Final moisture and consistency across the batch.</p></article><article><b>02 · Appearance</b><h3>Colour</h3><p>Instrumental or documented visual comparison.</p></article><article><b>03 · Aroma</b><h3>Volatile profile</h3><p>Relevant compounds and sensory interpretation.</p></article><article><b>04 · Safety</b><h3>Residues & microbes</h3><p>Tests selected with the laboratory and target requirements.</p></article><article><b>05 · Process</b><h3>Energy</h3><p>Fuel or electricity per unit of dried product.</p></article><article><b>06 · Adoption</b><h3>Practicality</h3><p>Cost, repair, workload and farmer evaluation.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="craft-v2-evidence"><div class="craft-v2-wrap"><div class="craft-v2-reveal"><p class="craft-v2-eyebrow">Evidence language</p><h2>Say exactly what we <em>know.</em></h2></div><div class="craft-v2-levels craft-v2-reveal"><article><b>Level 01</b><h3>Documented</h3><p>Directly observed, measured or supported by a reliable source.</p></article><article><b>Level 02</b><h3>Reported</h3><p>Attributed to a named source but not independently verified.</p></article><article><b>Level 03</b><h3>Testing</h3><p>A current research question with a defined method.</p></article><article><b>Level 04</b><h3>Unknown</h3><p>Kept visible instead of being filled with a convenient number.</p></article></div></div></section>
